{#
  KOTIVA cart — the reference's resources/views/cart/index.blade.php layout over Salla's cart.

  Salla's own APIs do the work: quantity changes post through salla.form.onChange
  ('cart.updateItem') and <salla-quantity-input cart-item-id>, removal through
  salla.cart.deleteItem(), checkout through salla.cart.submit() on Salla's hosted checkout
  (untouched). kotiva-cart.js repaints the figures in the reference format on every cart
  event. Coupons and Salla's cart hooks are kept for the merchant's apps.

  Known differences from the reference (docs/DECISIONS.md T-10): quantity is Salla's
  stepper (it saves on change, so there is no "Update" button), and the free-shipping bar,
  gifting and loyalty panels render only if the merchant enables those Salla features.

| Variable                 | Type        | Description                                   |
|--------------------------|-------------|-----------------------------------------------|
| cart.items[]             | CartItem[]  | id, product_id, url, product_name, product_image, quantity, max_quantity, price, total, is_available, is_hidden_quantity, type, options |
| cart.sub_total           | float       |                                               |
| cart.tax_amount          | float       |                                               |
| cart.discount            | float       |                                               |
| cart.total               | float       |                                               |
#}
{% extends "layouts.master" %}

{% block content %}
{% include 'components.kotiva.data' with {kotiva_view: 'components.kotiva.cart'} %}
{% endblock %}

{% block scripts %}
    <script>window.KOTIVA_THEME.taxInclusivePrices = {{ (store.settings.tax.taxable_prices_enabled ?? false) ? 'true' : 'false' }};</script>
    <script src="{{ 'kotiva-cart.js'|asset }}"></script>
{% endblock %}
